# This test checks the 'interface weakening' viscosity prefactor scheme of
# the visco plastic material model in a setup that combines particle- and
# field-advected compositional fields. The model setup is a simplified
# (coarser and shorter) version of the continental extension cookbook and is
# based on the test continental_extension_mixed_compositions_particles,
# which this test includes.
#
# The interface weakening scheme multiplies the viscosity of selected
# compositions by a prescribed factor in regions where the two compositions
# listed in 'Interface weakening compositions' are simultaneously present
# above a threshold value, i.e. within the numerically smeared transition
# band along the material interface between them. In this test, the
# viscosities of the upper and lower crust are multiplied by 1e-5 within
# the band along the upper crust--lower crust interface, creating a weak
# decoupling zone there, while the background, the mantle lithosphere and
# all single-composition regions retain their unmodified viscosities.
#
# The test verifies that the scheme is parsed correctly and runs in
# combination with particle-advected compositional fields, and that the
# weakening localizes deformation along the crustal interface.
# The exact value of the weakening factor is verified separately in the
# interface_weakening test, which computes the weakened viscosity 
# analytically.

include $ASPECT_SOURCE_DIR/tests/cookbooks/continental_extension_mixed_compositions_particles.prm

set End time                               = 10000

# Advect the lower crust with particles as well, so that both compositions
# of the weakened interface are tracked by particles.
subsection Compositional fields
  set Compositional field methods = particles, particles, particles, particles, field
  set Mapped particle properties  = plastic_strain: plastic_strain, \
                                    noninitial_plastic_strain: noninitial_plastic_strain, \
                                    crust_upper: initial crust_upper, \
                                    crust_lower: initial crust_lower
end

# All compositions tracked by particles must use the same finite element,
# so crust_lower uses the same polynomial degree and discontinuous
# discretization as the other particle-advected fields.
subsection Discretization
  set Composition polynomial degree                = 1,1,1,1,1
  set Use discontinuous composition discretization = true, true, true, true, true
end

subsection Material model
  subsection Visco Plastic
    set Viscosity prefactor scheme       = interface weakening
    set Interface weakening factors      = background: 1.0, crust_upper: 1e-5, crust_lower: 1e-5, mantle_lithosphere: 1.0
    set Interface weakening threshold    = 1e-6
    set Interface weakening compositions = crust_upper, crust_lower
  end
end
